The project assumes powerful actors will eventually try to manipulate it, so the defenses are structural \u2014 cryptographic attribution, append-only history, open scoring models, public traces, independent audits, provenance, independence analysis, reproducible snapshots, adversarial review, and alternative models over the same evidence \u2014 rather than trust in the operator."}, {"id": "constitution_article_xiii_corrections_do_not_erase_history", "label": "Article XIII \u2014 Corrections Do Not Erase History", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CONSTITUTION.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "constitution_article_xiv_humans_and_ai_are_contributors_not_oracles", "label": "Article XIV \u2014 Humans and AI Are Contributors, Not Oracles", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CONSTITUTION.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "constitution_article_xv_shared_evidence_and_personal_belief_are_separate_layers", "label": "Article XV \u2014 Shared Evidence and Personal Belief Are Separate Layers", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CONSTITUTION.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "constitution_article_xvi_disagreement_should_be_localized", "label": "Article XVI \u2014 Disagreement Should Be Localized", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CONSTITUTION.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "constitution_article_xvii_normative_claims_must_not_be_disguised_as_empirical_facts", "label": "Article XVII \u2014 Normative Claims Must Not Be Disguised as Empirical Facts", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CONSTITUTION.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "constitution_article_xviii_political_neutrality_is_structural", "label": "Article XVIII \u2014 Political Neutrality Is Structural", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CONSTITUTION.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "constitution_article_xix_transparency_over_persuasion", "label": "Article XIX \u2014 Transparency Over Persuasion", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CONSTITUTION.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "constitution_article_xx_models_may_change_evidence_must_endure", "label": "Article XX \u2014 Models May Change; Evidence Must Endure", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CONSTITUTION.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "constitution_article_xxi_research_should_be_cumulative", "label": "Article XXI \u2014 Research Should Be Cumulative", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CONSTITUTION.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "constitution_article_xxii_the_system_should_reveal_its_own_weaknesses", "label": "Article XXII \u2014 The System Should Reveal Its Own Weaknesses", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CONSTITUTION.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "constitution_article_xxiii_no_conclusion_is_immune_from_re_examination", "label": "Article XXIII \u2014 No Conclusion Is Immune From Re-Examination", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CONSTITUTION.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "constitution_article_xxiv_efficient_skepticism", "label": "Article XXIV \u2014 Efficient Skepticism", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CONSTITUTION.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Skepticism has value only when it can engage evidence, so the system distinguishes 'this claim is unsupported' from a refusal to accept any possible evidence, and 'unconventional' from 'contradicted by evidence'."}, {"id": "constitution_article_xxv_the_constitution_itself_is_amendable_but_not_silently", "label": "Article XXV \u2014 The Constitution Itself Is Amendable, But Not Silently", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CONSTITUTION.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An amendment must state what changed, why, what problem motivated it, what risks it introduces and whether it alters prior compatibility, so the project cannot drift into a different epistemic philosophy through undocumented implementation choices."}, {"id": "constitution_constitutional_test", "label": "The Constitutional Test (ten questions)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CONSTITUTION.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A 'no' to questions 1, 5, 6, 7, 8 or 9, or a 'yes' to 3 or 4, requires written justification or a design change; the answers are recorded so a feature cannot quietly trade away traceability for convenience."}, {"id": "constitution_foundational_statement", "label": "Foundational Statement", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CONSTITUTION.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "constitution_hash_integrity", "label": "constitution_hash published at /api/v1/meta", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CONSTITUTION.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "constitution_article_i_claims_are_not_truth", "target": "readme_galedra"